            <ArticleTitle>Clinical Guidance to Tattooing and Piercing Among Youth.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0882-5963(17)30635-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.pedn.2017.11.012</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tattoos, piercing, and scarification are increasingly common among young people. This paper reviews the first clinical report from the American Academy of Pediatrics which provides information for clinicians about these types of body modifications. The new report notes that complications are not common and that body modifications differ from non-suicidal self-injury. Additional references and information are provided to help clinicians can talk about these topics with patients and their families.</AbstractText>
